{
    "background_story": "Jedidiah was a brilliant architect with a passion for ancient structures. Growing up, he spent countless hours studying the pyramids of Egypt, fascinated by their precision and grandeur. As he honed his craft, Jedidiah became obsessed with building a modern marvel that rivaled the pyramids in scale and beauty. He spent years designing and refining his magnum opus, a pyramidically-shaped skyscraper that seemed to defy gravity. The Jedidiah Spire, as it came to be known, rose from the city skyline like a shining beacon, its pyramidical silhouette a testament to human ingenuity. Critics hailed it as a masterpiece, and Jedidiah's name became synonymous with innovative design. His creation stood as a monument to his unwavering dedication and creative vision.",
